			<div class="content" id="post-content-4852201">
									

<p>So, with regards to the world's backstory&#8230; I envisioned it as a &quot;paradise&quot; planet. It's got a warm climate, the seas are freshwater, and underwater food grows readily, even without cultivation. The original inhabitants were an aquatic race with an emphasis on trade. They were a friendly race, and in an attempt to facilitate trade, sent out these probes in the form of &quot;invitations&quot; to other aquatic worlds. I'm toying with the idea that they were thaumaturgists - explaining the anomalous teleportation - and the race went extinct when one of their rituals unfortunately went wrong - perhaps the one that turned their seas amber in the first place, in an attempt to make their world an &quot;anchor&quot; world for teleportation.</p>

