														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4852270">
									

<p>I've gotta disagree about it being tailored to human preferences. For one thing, the world is aquatic. That is decidedly not a paradise for someone who's stranded on a boat, completely dependent on a companion to retrieve food for them. The paradise is for aquatic creatures, as food is only readily available on the ocean floor, far out of reach of a surface-dwelling creature. The human is basically helpless, stranded on a small boat, which is something I intend to emphasize in the narrative.</p>
<p>As for communication&#8230; I don't suppose thaumaturgy can cover that? Though I hate the idea of &quot;magic did it&quot; as an answer for everything. Any suggestions?</p>

