			<div class="content" id="post-content-4852310">
									

<p>The main reason for the seas being freshwater is he's going to be out there for literally days. It's easier to explain away him drinking fresh water than staying alive for several days with no water, if the sea was salty. Plus, I also need him to keep a bottle of water with at least a little water from Earth in it for the climax of the story. It becomes a plot point that he's been able to survive off the water of the world. As for food, I WAS planning on there being a little trial and error, where a couple plants do make him sick, but he eventually finds a couple that at least sustain him. In the narrative, he's supposed to be surviving, just not thriving per se.</p>
<p>Up to this point, I wasn't going to say there was any particular connection to Earth; otherwise, they'd know the only sentient species on the planet is land-based, barring the anomalies that litter the SCP universe. I'm not thrilled about it, but at least if they're thaumaturgists who're able to transport other creatures from light years away, I'd imagine they also know some spells that allow for translation. Also saves me from having an additional explanation as to why the tritagonists of this story can communicate, if it's a blanket spell across the world. It's not a revolutionary solution, but at least it's consistent.</p>

							</div>

								
					
