<blockquote>
<p>The main reason for the seas being freshwater is he's going to be out there for literally days.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Sure, but the in-universe worldbuilding shouldn't just be wholly reliant on what you as the author need to happen for the story you want to tell. If the main reason something is present the way it is in-universe is &quot;because I need it to be that way&quot;, the setup is going to feel contrived and difficult to take seriously.</p>
<p>If there's not meant to be any connection to Earth, an easy fix is having the guy stranded in the &quot;Earth-adjacent welcoming area&quot; section of the world that's meant to receive organisms that live in Earth-like ocean biomes. Guy can do more exploring and find seams dividing that section from other oceans that would be more suitable to host species from different worlds, built specifically to encourage the interdimensional/interstellar trade.</p>

